 "summary": "The continuous Volterra existence theorem and the tail-integral identity `\u222b_{(x,\u221e)} g \u03a8\u1d4f = \u03a8(x)^{k+1}/(k+1)` have no counterpart in Mathlib or TauCeti; the closest relatives are the discrete `Summable.tsum_Ioi_mul_pow_tsum_Ioi_le` and `exists_discrete_volterra_solution`, and Mathlib's `integral_comp_mul_deriv_Ioi` needs a continuous derivative, which this identity does not assume. The proofs reuse Mathlib API (`AbsolutelyContinuousOnInterval.integral_deriv_eq_sub`, `continuousAt_of_dominated`, `continuousOn_tsum`, `hasSum_integral_of_summable_integral_norm`, `Real.summable_pow_div_factorial`) where it applies.",
